========================================
     COFFEE & WIFI — PROJECT README
========================================

This is a Flask web app that showcases cafes with data on power socket
availability, WiFi strength, and coffee quality. Users can browse
the list of cafes and add new ones through a validated form.

This project is from the Flask section of the course:
"100 Days of Code: The Complete Python Pro Bootcamp"


----------------------------------------
TABLE OF CONTENTS
----------------------------------------
1. Features
2. Requirements
3. Project Structure
4. Installation
5. How to Run
6. How to Use
7. Data Format
8. Routes & Forms
9. Credits
10. License


----------------------------------------
1. FEATURES
----------------------------------------
- Browse a curated list of work-friendly cafes
- View each cafe's opening hours, WiFi strength, coffee rating,
  and power socket availability
- Add a new cafe through a validated web form
- Data persisted in a simple CSV file (easy to edit by hand)
- Responsive Bootstrap 5 layout
- Optional cafe info link shown as a clickable "Link" in the table
- Emoji-based ratings for quick visual scanning


----------------------------------------
2. REQUIREMENTS
----------------------------------------
- Python 3.8+
- The following packages (see requirements.txt):

      Bootstrap_Flask==2.2.0
      Flask==2.3.2
      WTForms==3.0.1
      Flask_WTF==1.2.1
      Werkzeug==3.0.0

- A `.env` file or environment variable named SECRET_KEY
  (required by Flask-WTF for CSRF protection).


----------------------------------------
3. PROJECT STRUCTURE
----------------------------------------
.
|-- main.py                Flask app: routes and form definition
|-- requirements.txt       Python package dependencies
|-- cafe-data.csv          CSV file storing all cafe entries
|-- .env                   SECRET_KEY for Flask-WTF (do not commit!)
|-- templates/
|   |-- base.html          Layout template with Bootstrap + CSS links
|   |-- index.html         Landing page
|   |-- add.html           Add-a-cafe form page
|   |-- cafes.html         Table of all cafes
|-- static/
|   |-- css/
|       |-- styles.css     Custom styles
|-- README.txt             This file

Note: The app expects `logo.png` only if you add one; the provided
templates do not use an image, so no logo file is required.


----------------------------------------
4. INSTALLATION
----------------------------------------
1. Clone or download the project files into a folder.
2. (Recommended) Create and activate a virtual environment:

       python -m venv venv
       source venv/bin/activate      # macOS / Linux
       venv\Scripts\activate         # Windows

3. Install the dependencies:

       pip install -r requirements.txt

4. Set the SECRET_KEY environment variable. For example, create a
   .env file in the project root containing:

       SECRET_KEY=some-long-random-string

   Or export it directly:

       export SECRET_KEY="some-long-random-string"   # macOS / Linux
       set SECRET_KEY=some-long-random-string        # Windows


----------------------------------------
5. HOW TO RUN
----------------------------------------
From the project folder:

       python main.py

Then open your browser and go to:

       http://127.0.0.1:5000

The app runs in debug mode by default, so changes to .py and
.html files are picked up automatically.


----------------------------------------
6. HOW TO USE
----------------------------------------
HOME PAGE  ( / )
    Introduces the project and has a "Show Me!" button that
    takes you to the cafe list.

ALL CAFES  ( /cafes )
    Displays every cafe from cafe-data.csv in a table. Any cell
    whose value starts with "http" is rendered as a clickable
    "Link" instead of raw text.

ADD A CAFE ( /add )
    Fill in the form:
        - Cafe name
        - Cafe Info URL  (must be a valid URL)
        - Opening time   (free text, e.g. 8AM)
        - Closing time   (free text, e.g. 5:30PM)
        - Coffee rating  (☕️ ... ☕☕☕☕☕)
        - WiFi rating    (✘ ... 💪💪💪💪💪)
        - Power rating   (✘ ... 🔌🔌🔌🔌🔌)

    Submit the form to append the entry to cafe-data.csv; you are
    then redirected to the cafe list.


----------------------------------------
7. DATA FORMAT
----------------------------------------
cafe-data.csv uses a header row followed by one row per cafe:

    Cafe Name,Link,Open,Close,Coffee,Wifi,Power

Example:

    Cat & Mouse,https://example.com,10AM,12AM,☕☕☕,💪💪💪💪💪,🔌🔌🔌🔌🔌

Notes:
- The header row is read like any other row and therefore
  appears as the first table row on /cafes.
- Each new entry is appended with a leading newline, so the file
  always ends with a trailing newline.
- Editing entries can be done directly in the CSV file.


----------------------------------------
8. ROUTES & FORMS
----------------------------------------
Routes
    /          home()        Renders index.html
    /add       add_cafe()    GET: shows form. POST: validates,
                             appends to CSV, redirects to /cafes.
    /cafes     cafes()       Reads CSV and renders cafes.html

CafeForm fields
    cafe            StringField, required
    location        StringField, required + URL validation
    open            StringField, required
    close           StringField, required
    coffee_rating   SelectField, required
    wifi_rating     SelectField, required
    power_rating    SelectField, required
    submit          SubmitField

All forms are rendered using `bootstrap/form.html`'s render_form
macro, which automatically applies Bootstrap styling and shows
validation errors.


